====================================================================================
LRC(14) cover  <->  cycle-space / even-subgraph  bridge test  (kind-pasteur S?)
====================================================================================

--- FORM (1): is Lambda(E) a Z cycle space?  rank accounting ---
  Lattice {n: sum n_i e_i=0} has rank k-1 (one linear constraint).
  Affine {+ sum n_i=0} has rank k-2.  A graph cycle space has rank |E|-|V|+c.
  consec {1..8} (+0)       k=9: lin-relation-rank=8 (=k-1), affine-relation-rank=7 (=k-2)
  consec {1..13} (full)    k=14: lin-relation-rank=13 (=k-1), affine-relation-rank=12 (=k-2)
  AP-line {0,2,4,6,8}      k=5: lin-relation-rank=4 (=k-1), affine-relation-rank=3 (=k-2)
  Sidon-ish {0,1,4,9,11}   k=5: lin-relation-rank=4 (=k-1), affine-relation-rank=3 (=k-2)
  two-large {0,1,500}      k=3: lin-relation-rank=2 (=k-1), affine-relation-rank=1 (=k-2)
  READ: Lambda is the kernel of a 1x k (or 2x k) integer matrix = a COROTOR /
        a rank-(k-1) lattice.  It IS a 'cycle space' of the SPEED MATROID
        (column matroid of [e_i]); but that matroid is uniform U_{1,k} (or the
        affine point config), NOT the graphic cycle space of a fixed graph.

