--- FORM (4): the doubling (QR/NQR) split = the Euler even/odd factor swap? ---
  doubling z->2z on Z/7 has order 3; QR(7)={1,2,4}, NQR(7)={3,5,6}, fixes 0.
  Euler: (1+x^n)=(1-x^{2n})/(1-x^n) cancels EVEN powers (the 2-power tower).
  Speed e=2^a*b (Glaisher): doubling a runner multiplies its sector by 2.
  consec {1..8} (+0)      : covAll=0.4162 covQR=0.5923 covNQR=0.5551  QR*NQR=0.3288  2-exps_present=[0, 1, 2, 3]
  consec {1..13} (full)   : (skipped)
  AP-line {0,2,4,6,8}     : covAll=0.0000 covQR=0.1905 covNQR=0.1190  QR*NQR=0.0227  2-exps_present=[1, 2, 3]
  Sidon-ish {0,1,4,9,11}  : covAll=0.0000 covQR=0.0570 covNQR=0.1122  QR*NQR=0.0064  2-exps_present=[0, 2]
  two-large {0,1,500}     : covAll=0.0000 covQR=0.0000 covNQR=0.0000  QR*NQR=0.0000  2-exps_present=[0, 2]

--- VERDICT SUMMARY (printed; full prose in agent return) ---
  (1) Lambda = cycle space of the SPEED MATROID (uniform/affine), not graphic. STRUCTURAL.
  (2) GF(2) even-subgraph dim = k-1 (lin) / k-2 (aff): a real parity space, but the
      cover measure does NOT factor through it (real coeffs e_i, not just parities). ANALOGY.
  (3) (-1)^{|T|} Mayer sign == the OCF inclusion-exclusion sign: SAME parity algebra. REAL.
  (4) doubling QR/NQR split is positively correlated, NO clean factorization. NUMEROLOGY-ish.
